{% set message = symbol("ts:spectrum-ts#Message") %}
{% set space = symbol("ts:spectrum-ts#Space") %}
{% set honoOptions = symbol("ts:@spectrum-ts/hono#SpectrumPluginOptions") %}
{% set expressOptions = symbol("ts:@spectrum-ts/express#SpectrumPluginOptions") %}
{% set elysiaOptions = symbol("ts:@spectrum-ts/elysia#SpectrumPluginOptions") %}

`app.webhook()` lets you receive messages through HTTP `POST` requests instead of the `app.messages` stream. It handles all Spectrum delivery formats through the same method:

| | Native Spectrum webhook | Standard project webhook | Direct Fusor webhook |
|---|---|---|---|
| Body | Normalized JSON | `message.received` JSON preserving the provider request | Protobuf envelope preserving the provider request |
| Auth | Legacy HMAC with `webhookSecret` | Standard Webhooks v1 with `standardWebhookSecret` | Platform's own signature via provider `verify()` |
| Requires a Fusor provider | No | Yes | Yes |

Standard project webhooks are detected by the `webhook-*` headers. Native JSON and direct Fusor protobuf deliveries are distinguished by payload shape. Your handler receives the same `(space, message)` pair in every case.

## Configuring signing secrets

Pass the Standard `whsec_` secret returned when you register the endpoint. Keep `webhookSecret` only while receiving native or migration-era legacy signatures:

```ts
const app = await Spectrum({
  projectId: process.env.PROJECT_ID!,
  projectSecret: process.env.PROJECT_SECRET!,
  providers: [imessage.config()],
  standardWebhookSecret: process.env.SPECTRUM_STANDARD_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
  webhookSecret: process.env.SPECTRUM_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
});
```

Both options fall back to their matching environment variables (`SPECTRUM_STANDARD_WEBHOOK_SECRET` and `SPECTRUM_WEBHOOK_SECRET`); an explicit option takes precedence. Pass the complete `whsec_...` value—the SDK removes the prefix and Base64-decodes the key internally. A signed delivery that arrives without a matching configured secret is answered `500`.

## Registering and managing project webhooks

The public `cloud` client covers endpoint registration, subscriptions, enable/disable controls, secret rotation, stable egress IPs, delivery history, replay, and deletion:

```ts
import { cloud } from "spectrum-ts";

const endpoint = await cloud.createWebhook(projectId, projectSecret, {
  webhookUrl: "https://agent.example.com/spectrum/webhook",
  eventTypes: ["message.received"],
  failureNotificationEmail: "alerts@example.com",
});

// Returned only at creation. Persist this full value in your secret manager.
const standardSigningSecret = endpoint.standardSigningSecret;

await cloud.updateWebhook(projectId, projectSecret, endpoint.id, {
  enabled: false,
});

const rotated = await cloud.rotateWebhookSecret(
  projectId,
  projectSecret,
  endpoint.id,
  { overlapSeconds: 86_400 }
);
// Deploy rotated.standardSigningSecret before the overlap expires.
```

During the overlap, `webhook-signature` contains signatures for both secrets, so either the old or new configured secret verifies. Use `cloud.getWebhookEgressIps(...)` for network allowlists. `cloud.listWebhookDeliveries(...)`, `cloud.replayWebhookDelivery(...)`, and `cloud.replayFailedWebhookDeliveries(...)` expose the retained delivery history and bounded replay controls.

To verify a Standard Webhooks request without routing it through `app.webhook()`, use the exact raw bytes:

```ts
import {
  parseStandardWebhookEvent,
  verifyStandardWebhookSignature,
} from "spectrum-ts";

const rawBody = new Uint8Array(await request.arrayBuffer());
const verification = verifyStandardWebhookSignature({
  rawBody,
  headers: request.headers,
  secret: process.env.SPECTRUM_STANDARD_WEBHOOK_SECRET!,
});

if (!verification.ok) {
  return new Response(verification.reason, { status: 401 });
}

const event = parseStandardWebhookEvent(rawBody);
```

## Receiving deliveries

Call `app.webhook()` from your HTTP server's `POST` route. The method has two overloads:

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="Web Request (Hono / Bun.serve / Workers)">
    ```ts
    server.post("/spectrum/webhook", (c) =>
      app.webhook(c.req.raw, async (space, message) => {
        if (message.content.type === "text") {
          await space.send(`echo: ${message.content.text}`);
        }
      })
    );
    ```
  </Tab>
  <Tab title="Raw (Express / Node)">
    ```ts
    server.post(
      "/spectrum/webhook",
      express.raw({ type: "*/*" }),
      async (req, res) => {
        const result = await app.webhook(
          { body: req.body, headers: req.headers },
          async (space, message) => {
            if (message.content.type === "text") {
              await space.send(`echo: ${message.content.text}`);
            }
          }
        );
        res.status(result.status).set(result.headers).send(Buffer.from(result.body));
      }
    );
    ```
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

The handler is invoked **fire-and-forget** — it runs after the HTTP response is sent. A throw is logged, never surfaced. Dedupe on `message.id` for exactly-once side effects.

<Warning>
Pass the raw body bytes. The HMAC is computed over the exact bytes on the wire. If your framework parses the body to JSON and you re-stringify it, the bytes change and verification fails.
</Warning>

## Framework adapters

First-party adapters mount the endpoint for you and handle raw-body parsing correctly. Install the adapter package and its framework only when you use it.

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="Hono">
    ```ts
    import { Hono } from "hono";
    import { Spectrum } from "spectrum-ts";
    import { imessage } from "spectrum-ts/providers/imessage";
    import { spectrum } from "@spectrum-ts/hono";

    const app = await Spectrum({
      projectId: process.env.PROJECT_ID!,
      projectSecret: process.env.PROJECT_SECRET!,
      providers: [imessage.config()],
      standardWebhookSecret: process.env.SPECTRUM_STANDARD_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
      webhookSecret: process.env.SPECTRUM_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
    });

    const server = new Hono().route(
      "/",
      spectrum({
        app,
        onMessage: async (space, message) => {
          if (message.content.type === "text") {
            await space.send(`echo: ${message.content.text}`);
          }
        },
      })
    );

    export default server;
    ```

    <Accordion title="SpectrumPluginOptions" description="{{ honoOptions.doc.summary }}">
